flowchart TB
  accTitle: Inside a container box
  accDescr: The worker starts the box from the project’s image through the Docker socket, with CPU and memory limits, and passes the job’s secrets as environment variables. The box mounts the job’s clone, the read-only toolbox and guidelines, and a cache. Its network is Docker’s `bridge` by default.
  runner["Worker: the job runner"]
  subgraph box["Box: a container from the project’s image"]
    direction TB
    ws["`/workspace`<br>the job’s clone"]
    tb["`/opt/beeverforge-toolbox`<br>harness binaries, read-only"]
    gl["`/opt/beeverforge-guidelines`<br>guidelines, read-only"]
    cache["`/cache`<br>dependency cache"]
    ws ~~~ tb
    gl ~~~ cache
  end
  net["Network reachable from the box"]
  runner -->|"`docker run` with CPU and memory limits,<br>then `docker exec`, through the Docker socket"| box
  runner -.->|"secrets as environment variables"| box
  box -->|"`bridge` by default"| net
